MiniMax-H3 weight converters, vendored

Source: the h3 engine repository, branch native, commit 03881cc, copied
unchanged without history, with the runtime they convert for
(runtime/video/VENDORED):

  h3 tools/convert_{dit,vae,preview,prep,audio}.py  -> install/video/
  h3 h3/common.py, config.py, safetensors.py        -> install/video/h3/

install/videos.py runs them once per installation, with install/video as the
working directory and import path, into the prepared-weight cache
(video/<key>, the key hashing these files and the source commits): the DiT
blocks, QKFIX tensors, io tensors and SSD stream image and the request
preparation's tensors per variant, the W8 video VAE, the audio VAE and TAEH3.
They read numpy and safetensors only, but for the video VAE's rotary tables,
which convert_vae.py computes with MLX (H3_MLX_PORT); give the installer an
interpreter that has MLX with --converter-python.
